WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.872
Hello.

2
00:00:01.872 --> 00:00:08.328
In this lesson we learn the simplest and most widely used method: separating the variables.

3
00:00:08.328 --> 00:00:15.600
A virus spreading in a network, tea cooling down, radioactive decay — all of these are solved this way.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:22.550
By the end you will not only solve the equation but also find the solutions that get lost when we divide.

5
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.768
An equation is separable when the right side splits into two factors,

6
00:00:27.768 --> 00:00:31.896
one depending only on x and the other only on y.

7
00:00:31.896 --> 00:00:40.752
Then we move everything with y to the left and everything with x to the right: d y over g of y equals f of x times d x.

8
00:00:40.752 --> 00:00:45.590
Then we integrate both sides and add a single constant C.

9
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.160
Example: y prime equals x times y squared.

10
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.496
Here f is x and g is y squared.

11
00:00:53.496 --> 00:00:58.152
An important step before dividing: set g equal to zero.

12
00:00:58.152 --> 00:01:02.544
If y squared is zero, then y is identically zero.

13
00:01:02.544 --> 00:01:07.224
Check it: the left side is zero and the right side is zero.

14
00:01:07.224 --> 00:01:10.704
So y identically zero is a solution.

15
00:01:10.704 --> 00:01:13.622
We write it down right away.

16
00:01:13.872 --> 00:01:20.304
Now assume y is not zero and separate: d y over y squared equals x d x.

17
00:01:20.304 --> 00:01:26.400
The integral on the left is minus one over y, on the right it is half of x squared.

18
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.896
We add one constant.

19
00:01:28.896 --> 00:01:34.886
The result: minus one over y equals x squared over two plus C one.

20
00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:42.072
Solve for y: y equals minus two over x squared plus C, where C is two C one.

21
00:01:42.072 --> 00:01:47.352
The full answer has two parts: this formula and y identically zero.

22
00:01:47.352 --> 00:01:53.088
Notice that y identically zero does not come from the formula for any finite C.

23
00:01:53.088 --> 00:01:58.214
Had we not written it down beforehand, it would have been lost completely.

24
00:01:58.464 --> 00:02:00.960
Look at the direction field.

25
00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.896
Exactly on the y axis, x is zero,

26
00:02:04.896 --> 00:02:10.896
so the segments there are horizontal; near the y axis their slopes are merely small.

27
00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:17.304
The x axis itself is also an integral curve: it is the solution y identically zero.

28
00:02:17.304 --> 00:02:22.848
The curves above and below never cross it, as the uniqueness theorem guarantees.

29
00:02:22.848 --> 00:02:27.086
The lower curve is the solution with C equal to two.

30
00:02:27.336 --> 00:02:29.640
Now test yourself.

31
00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.696
Find the constant solutions of the equation on the screen.

32
00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:38.352
Hint: set the right side equal to zero and check each root.

33
00:02:38.352 --> 00:02:42.566
After choosing an answer, read the explanation.
